  "analysis": "We need to count how many ways to replace zeros in a sequence of length n (each element is 0, 2, or 4) with 2 or 4 so that the described 1D 2048-like game on an infinite stripe reaches a tile of value at least 2^k. The process can be modeled as binary addition of tile levels: each tile level i corresponds to value 2^i (i >= 1). The stripe state after some steps never contains two tiles of the same level; instead, adding a tile of level t is equivalent to adding 1 at binary position t to a bitmask representing which levels are present (with bits 1..k-1). If a carry propagates beyond level k-1 (i reaches k), we would create a tile of level k, i.e., reach 2^k, which means a winning sequence. Therefore, to count non-winning sequences (never reach 2^k), we can perform a DP over bitmasks of length m = k-1, processing the sequence left to right and applying the binary-add-t operation. For positions with a fixed 2 or 4, only the corresponding t is allowed; for zeros, both t=1 and t=2 options are allowed. The number of valid non-winning sequences is the sum of DP states after processing all n positions. The total number of sequences is 2^(number_of_zeros). The answer is (total - non_winning) mod 1e9+7.

Constraints are small enough for a DP over 2^(k-1) masks (k <= 11 -> at most 2^10 = 1024 states) and n up to 2000. This yields O(n * 2^(k-1)) transitions, easily within limits. The implementation below follows this approach.

Key points:
- Represent mask bits as bit (i-1) corresponding to level i for i in [1, m].
- When adding t, perform carry: while bit (p-1) is 1, clear it and advance p; if p <= m, set bit (p-1); else carry would reach level k (overflow) -> skip this transition for the non-winning DP.
- After processing all positions, non-winning sequences are sum of DP states; total sequences is 2^(#zeros). Answer = (total - non_winning) mod MOD.
",
  "plan": "1) Implement a C++17 program that reads n, k and the sequence. 2) Use m = k-1 and a DP array of size 2^m representing masks of levels 1..m. 3) Initialize dp[0] = 1. 4) For each position, compute ndp by considering possible t values (if a[i] == 0 then t in {1,2}, else fixed t). 5) For each mask and t, compute the new_mask via the carry propagation described; if carry would overflow to level k, skip (as this path would be winning). 6) After processing all positions, sum dp to obtain non-winning sequences. 7) Compute total = 2^(count_zero). 8) Answer = (total - non_winning) mod MOD. 9) Test with provided samples to ensure correctness.",
  "commands": [
    {
      "keystrokes": "cat > main.cpp << 'CPP'\n#include <bits/stdc++.h>\nusing namespace std;\n\nconst long long MOD = 1000000007LL;\n\nint main(){\n    ios::sync_with_stdio(false);\n    cin.tie(nullptr);\n\n    int n, k;\n    if(!(cin >> n >> k)) return 0;\n    vector<int> a(n);\n    for(int i = 0; i < n; ++i) cin >> a[i];\n\n    int m = k - 1; // number of bits to track (levels 1..k-1)\n    if(m < 0) m = 0; // safety\n    int totalZeros = 0;\n    for(int x : a) if(x == 0) totalZeros++;\n\n    int maxMask = 1 << m;\n    vector<long long> dp(maxMask, 0), ndp(maxMask, 0);\n    dp[0] = 1; // start with empty stripe (no tiles of levels 1..m)\n\n    for(int pos = 0; pos < n; ++pos){\n        fill(ndp.begin(), ndp.end(), 0);\n        // determine possible t-values for this position\n        vector<int> ts;\n        if(a[pos] == 0) ts = {1, 2};\n        else if(a[pos] == 2) ts = {1};\n        else if(a[pos] == 4) ts = {2};\n        else ts.clear();\n        for(int mask = 0; mask < maxMask; ++mask){\n            long long cur = dp[mask];\n            if(!cur) continue;\n            for(int t : ts){\n                int new_mask = mask;\n                int p = t; // target bit position (1-based level)\n                // carry while bit p-1 is 1\n                while(p <= m && ((new_mask >> (p-1)) & 1)){\n                    new_mask &= ~(1 << (p-1));\n                    ++p;\n                }\n                if(p <= m){\n                    new_mask |= (1 << (p-1));\n                    ndp[new_mask] += cur;\n                    if(ndp[new_mask] >= MOD) ndp[new_mask] -= MOD;\n                } else {\n                    // would overflow to level k (2^k), i.e., winning sequence; skip for non-winning DP\n                }\n            }\n        }\n        dp.swap(ndp);\n    }\n\n    long long nonWin = 0;\n    for(int mask = 0; mask < maxMask; ++mask){\n        nonWin += dp[mask];\n        if(nonWin >= MOD) nonWin -= MOD;\n    }\n\n    long long total = 1;\n    for(int i = 0; i < totalZeros; ++i){\n        total = (total * 2) % MOD;\n    }\n\n    long long ans = (total - nonWin) % MOD;\n    if(ans < 0) ans += MOD;\n    cout << ans << \"\\n\";\n    return 0;\n}\nCPP\n",
